From 4582aac7ac8577806b7d193bfe05484b29456b03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:29:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] radv/ps4: host pointers in direct memory mapped for the
 GPU

VK_EXT_external_memory_host imports memory the application already
mapped for the GPU: direct memory whose every mapping in the range gives
the GPU read and write access, below its 40-bit address limit, as
sceKernelVirtualQuery reports it. The PS4 grants the GPU no other memory,
so anything else is refused. An imported buffer stays the application's.

VideoOut's framebuffers reach RADV this way (wsi_common_videoout.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KvB274h9yAsuA8U9fnRoFR
